This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**
   - **Message 1:** "Please work on issue 1482." — a dispatch prompt in the Claudinite canon repo (`missingbulb/Claudinite`), designated branch `claude/issue-1482-dmv0zo`. Issue [#1482](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/1482): PR #1466's janitor rule F widening shipped under `claudinite-tasks` version `60830.5`, which #1464 had already published, so no member could ever receive it. A prior owner comment on the issue had established the mechanism exactly (two branches racing to the same next version; `pack.mjs` auto-merges on identical bytes) and deliberately left the design call between three options: merge-queue ordering, a world-scope uniqueness assertion over `VERSIONS.md`, or a non-literal bump.
   - **Message 2:** "Was the problem in versions.md ? Or was the problem that code was changes and the version wasn't upgraded?" — a correction: the defect is content landing without the version moving; the duplicated `VERSIONS.md` row is only a symptom. Intent: measure the real thing.
   - **Message 3:** "I don't understand the PR. What fixes the problem of not upgrading the version? Do you want another check for the versions.md file? Do it in another PR." — split the work: PR #1523 must be only the fix for the version-not-upgraded problem; the `VERSIONS.md` check (and its repairs) goes in a separate PR.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Claudinite pack delivery: a member re-vendors `packs/<id>/` only where `planPackUpdates` sees `installed.packVersions[id] < pack.version`; the version number *is* the delivery signal and the fleet's name for a set of bytes. The engine tree, by contrast, vendors wholesale every converge (so `engine/RELEASES.md` has no equivalent collision failure mode).
   - Check scopes: `work` (the diff vs the branch's merge base, run by `engine/checks/ci-work-scope.mjs`) and `world` (the tree, run by `engine/checks/check_the_world.mjs`). `ci-work-scope.decide()` skips when `HEAD === origin/main`, which is why a push to main judged no change.
   - Structural rule discovery: canon-curation's `workRules/` and `worldRules/` directories are discovered structurally (the manifest doesn't restate its tree).
   - Version format (`engine/version.mjs`): date-anchored `<day>.<seq>` strings; `parseVersion` → `{day, seq}`; `formatVersion({day,seq})`; `compareVersions`, `versionsEqual`, `nextVersion`, `VERSION_SOURCE`.
   - Repo conventions applied: issue → branch → PR with `Closes #N` in the body; `Comment class:` declaration line on the first substantive reply; see-it-fail before landing a check; prove a check silent against the *real* tree, not just fixtures; catalog row in the pack README; local packs (`.claudinite/local/packs/`) vendor nowhere and need no version bump; `VERSIONS.md` edits are excluded from `packsTouched`.

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/pack-delivery-on-main.mjs`** (new; the PR #1523 deliverable — the actual fix). Re-asks the existing `pack-version-bumped` rule on `main` against what `main` held before the push, which is the only point where both racing branches exist.
     ```js
     import { execFileSync } from 'node:child_process';
     import { realpathSync } from 'node:fs';
     import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';
     import rule from './workRules/pack-version-bumped.mjs';

     const git = (root, ...args) => {
       try { return execFileSync('git', args, { cwd: root, encoding: 'utf8' }); } catch { return null; }
     };
     const at = (root, ref, file) => git(root, 'show', `${ref}:${file}`);

     export function resolveBefore(root, { before = null } = {}) {
       const resolvable = (ref) => (ref && git(root, 'rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', `${ref}^{commit}`) ? ref : null);
       return resolvable(before) || resolvable('HEAD^');
     }
     export function contextBetween(root, base, head = 'HEAD') {
       const changed = (git(root, 'diff', '--name-only', `${base}..${head}`) || '').split('\n').filter(Boolean);
       return { changedFiles: changed, read: (f) => at(root, head, f), readBase: (f) => at(root, base, f) };
     }
     export function judge(root, { before = null } = {}) {
       const base = resolveBefore(root, { before });
       if (!base) return { base: null, findings: [] };
       return { base, findings: rule.run(contextBetween(root, base)) };
     }
     ```
     CLI (guarded by `realpathSync(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)`) reads `process.env.GITHUB_EVENT_BEFORE`, exits 0 on OK/nothing-to-judge and 1 with per-finding output on failure. Header comment explains why a branch cannot see the collision, why only this rule runs on main (branch-shaped rules have no answer on a squashed merge commit), and the `before` fallback rationale.

   - **`.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/test/pack-delivery-on-main.test.mjs`** (new, 5 tests, all passing): collision detected; content landing with its own version is clean; the push's own base is judged (`judge(root,{before})` clean vs `judge(root)` flagging); unresolvable `before` falls back to `HEAD^`; a first commit has no previous main. Uses `makeRepo`, `cleanup`, `git`, `writeFiles` from `engine-tests/helpers.mjs`.

   - **`.github/workflows/ci.yml`** (modified): new step inserted before "Growth write-surface gate":
     ```yaml
     - name: Pack delivery (push to main)
       if: github.event_name == 'push'
       env:
         GITHUB_EVENT_BEFORE: ${{ github.event.before }}
       run: node .claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/pack-delivery-on-main.mjs
     ```

   - **`.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/worldRules/pack-version-claimed-once.mjs`** (new; now on the *second* branch/PR only). World-scope blocking rule `pack-version-claimed-once`: no two rows of a pack's `VERSIONS.md` claim the same version.
     ```js
     const logs = ctx.files.filter((f) => f.startsWith('packs/')
       && f.endsWith(`/${VERSIONS_FILENAME}`) && f.split('/').length === 3);
     for (const file of logs) {
       const seen = new Map();
       for (const { version, line } of rowVersions(ctx.read(file))) {
         const parsed = parseVersion(version);
         if (!parsed) continue;
         const key = formatVersion(parsed);
         if (!seen.has(key)) { seen.set(key, line); continue; }
         findings.push(finding(rule, { file, line, what: `version ${version} is claimed by two rows (also line ${seen.get(key)}), ...`, fix: ... }));
       }
     }
     ```
     Header comment now positions it as the **record** half, with `pack-delivery-on-main.mjs` as the delivery half, and notes the engine has no twin because the engine vendors wholesale.

   - **`.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/workRules/pack-version-bumped.mjs`** (modified on the second branch only; reverted to main's state on the #1523 branch): added `export function rowVersions(text)` returning `[{version, line}]` and rebuilt `versionRecorded` as `rowVersions(text).some((claim) => versionsEqual(claim.version, version))`.

   - **`.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/test/pack-version-claimed-once.test.mjs`** (new, second branch, 6 tests) including a real-tree test that reads every `git ls-files 'packs/*/VERSIONS.md'` and asserts no findings.

   - **`packs/claudinite-dashboard/VERSIONS.md`, `packs/claudinite-growth/VERSIONS.md`, `packs/claudinite-tasks/VERSIONS.md`** (second branch): four duplicate rows folded into one row per version, each with the appended clause "Two changes claimed this number (#1482), so a member that converged between the two merges took only one of them; both are in every mount from the next version on."

   - **`.claudinite/local/packs/canon-curation/README.md`**: catalog row `| Landed pack edit is deliverable | [pack-delivery-on-main.mjs](pack-delivery-on-main.mjs), CI on every push to main |` on the #1523 branch; `| One pack version, one tree | check pack-version-claimed-once |` on the #1527 branch.

4. **Errors and fixes:**
   - **`formatVersion` misuse** — the first run of `pack-version-claimed-once` emitted ~144 findings all keyed `undefined.undefined`, because row values are raw literals (`'60830.5'`) while `formatVersion` expects `{day, seq}`. Fixed by `parseVersion(version)` first, `continue` on null, and printing the raw literal in the message. After the fix the real tree produced exactly the 4 genuine collisions.
   - **Full-suite Bash timeout** — `node --test $(git ls-files '*.test.mjs')` exceeded the 2-minute default and was killed (exit 143); re-run with `timeout: 420000` (~115–130s, 2844→2849 passing).
   - **`check_the_work.mjs` with no base printed nothing** — the work scope needs committed changes and a base; resolved by committing first and running `node engine/checks/ci-work-scope.mjs --branch <branch>`.
   - **User correction (message 2)** — I had measured the symptom (`VERSIONS.md` duplication) rather than the defect (content changed without a version move). Fixed by adding the main-side delivery gate and verifying it fires on the real commit `7a73464a`.
   - **User correction (message 3)** — the PR mixed two things and did not lead with the fix. Fixed by rebuilding the `claude/issue-1482-dmv0zo` branch from `origin/main` with only the gate, force-pushing with `--force-with-lease`, rewriting PR #1523, and moving the log work to issue #1527 / branch `claude/issue-1527-versions-log` / PR #1529.
   - **Shell cwd reset** — after `cd` into the scratchpad clone, the harness reported "Shell cwd was reset to /home/user/Claudinite" (the known local rule); no impact since each command carried its own `cd`.

5. **Problem Solving:**
   - Diagnosed why `pack-version-bumped` could not fire on #1466: it is `scope: 'work'` against the branch's own merge base, where the version *had* moved; the collision only exists once both branches are on `main`.
   - Rejected merge-queue / "require branches up to date" (a platform setting — last resort per the repo's standing decisions — and at twelve `claudinite-tasks` versions in 21 hours every PR would need serial update + CI re-run) and a non-literal bump (replaces the number the whole delivery mechanism is written against).
   - Verified the chosen gate against real history: at `7a73464a` four shipping files changed while `pack.mjs` stayed at its parent's `60830.5`; the gate exits 1 naming the file, version, and the `60831.1` remedy.
   - Answered the issue's open question ("worth checking whether any other pair collided"): four collisions across three packs, not one.
   - Confirmed the issue's "immediate remedy" (force `fleet-baseline`, wake `task-janitor`) is moot: #1472 shipped `60830.6` and the pack is now at `60831.5`.

6. **All user messages:**
   - "Please work on issue 1482."
   - "Was the problem in versions.md ? Or was the problem that code was changes and the version wasn't upgraded?"
   - "I don't understand the PR. What fixes the problem of not upgrading the version? Do you want another check for the versions.md file? Do it in another PR."
   - (Standing owner interaction preferences injected at session start, to keep applying: end every turn with a blockquote callout, never hedged prose; "LGTM" merges the change at hand via `merge-to-main`, approving that change only; "bump version" raises the project version; link every source-controlled document edited and every issue/PR number; ask every decision or approval through an `AskUserQuestion` popup, never prose; enclose anything the owner will lift elsewhere in one delimited block; prefix a prompt written for another session with a Claude-wrote-it disclaimer; open a pull request right after committing to a branch, unasked; when handing over a PR, describe the folders touched in a text box, non-test folders only, ignoring READMEs, comment-only changes and version/changelog rows; keep working through a multi-step plan without pausing for per-step approval, stopping only for world-reaching or owner-only decisions; never schedule a self check-in to poll a PR.)

7. **Pending Tasks:**
   - Report back to the user on the completed split (this had not yet been done when the summary was requested): PR [#1523](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/1523) now carries only the delivery gate; issue [#1527](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/1527) and PR [#1529](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/1529) carry the `VERSIONS.md` check plus the four row repairs.
   - Both PRs await owner review ("LGTM" would merge the one at hand).

8. **Current Work:**
   Immediately before the summary request I completed the split the user asked for in message 3:
   - Rebuilt `claude/issue-1482-dmv0zo` from `origin/main` containing only `pack-delivery-on-main.mjs`, its test, the `ci.yml` step, and its README row; commit `58dd042` ("Ask the delivery question again on main, where both branches are visible", `Refs #1482`); force-pushed with `--force-with-lease`. Verified: canon-curation tests 44 pass, work scope clean (4 changed files), `check_the_world` 0 blocking.
   - Rewrote PR #1523's title to "Ask the delivery question again on main, where both branches are visible" and its body to open with "**What fixes the problem:** CI now runs `pack-version-bumped` a second time — on every push to `main`, against what `main` held before that push," including the real `7a73464a` failure output and a "Not in this PR" section pointing at the split-out work.
   - Created issue #1527 ("Four pack versions are claimed by two VERSIONS.md rows each") with the four-collision table.
   - Created branch `claude/issue-1527-versions-log` off `origin/main`, cherry-picked the saved log commit, reworded the rule header to make it the record half, amended the message to "One pack version, one row of its log … Refs #1527", verified (canon-curation tests pass, world 0 blocking, full suite 2846 pass), pushed, and opened PR #1529 ("One pack version, one row of its log", `Closes #1527`, `Comment class: other`).

9. **Optional Next Step:**
   Reply to the user in prose (no further code work) summarizing the split, per their instruction "What fixes the problem of not upgrading the version? Do you want another check for the versions.md file? Do it in another PR." — stating plainly that PR [#1523](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/1523) is now solely the fix (CI re-runs `pack-version-bumped` on every push to `main` against `github.event.before`, which fires on the real `7a73464a` commit), that the `VERSIONS.md` check and the four row repairs moved to issue [#1527](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/issues/1527) / PR [#1529](https://github.com/missingbulb/Claudinite/pull/1529), with the required folders-touched text box for each PR and a closing blockquote callout listing both PRs as still open for review.

If you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-home-user-Claudinite/fdee6411-fc63-5422-a5e9-55f7ae5953fd.jsonl
